  "chapter": 609,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 39 Chapter 609\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 2977-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the executive law and the public health law, in\n        relation to certain questions regarding veterans on intake forms\n        for admission and residency\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  The goal of this bill is to identify those individuals who are  veter-\nans  and  are  currently  living in homeless shelters, nursing homes, or\nassisted living facilities, to ensure the Division of Veterans  Services\nhas  a better chance of assisting these individuals to receive the bene-\nfits that they have earned and deserve.\n \n  While there are several technical concerns that need to  be  addressed\nto ensure this legislation will have its intended impact, I have reached\nan  agreement  with  the Legislature to pass legislation in the upcoming\nsession that will address these issues and  help  ensure  that  as  many\nveterans as possible are receiving their benefits. For example, the bill\nonly addresses assisted living residences, but doesn't as drafted recog-\nnize that there are other categories of adult care facilities that might\nalso  house  veterans.  On  the basis of that agreement, I am pleased to\nsign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
